{
	title: 'Own plain metadata updates in sessions',
	spec: 'sessions.update(id, fields) applies a partial metadata update, removes explicitly undefined fields, saves synchronously, then broadcasts one metadata snapshot. Save errors propagate without broadcasting. Budget, card overrides, hal/tool card defaults, and naming use this operation instead of coordinating liveFiles and host themselves. Existing validation, names, replies, persistence and event ordering remain unchanged. History-sensitive metadata paths keep their existing sequencing. The bounded refactor must reduce production source lines including callers and the shared implementation.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Compared a save-and-publish helper with an operation that owns mutation. Chose update(id, fields), restricted by TypeScript to slots, blocks and naming fields so callers cannot use it for history-backed cwd/model/autoclose changes. Explicit undefined deletes a field; omission preserves it. No timers, watchers or retained state were added; work is proportional to the supplied fields. Existing persistence still owns writes.',
		'Measured the five changed production files against HEAD: 452 to 440 nonblank noncomment source lines (-12); 526 to 516 physical lines (-10). One durable save-before-notify regression adds 30 source lines (31 physical), so production plus tests grows by 18 source lines. Existing caller tests and shared host tests: 53 pass. Formatting and changed-file lint pass. Two convention failures and type errors remain unchanged from baseline; the type baseline was verified with these six files at HEAD. Experiment remains uncommitted pending user evaluation. Removing naming.save is a plugin-visible API change: callers can use sessions.update(id, {}); declare it and the new update API if retained.',
		'Accepted by the user. This implements the retained metadata candidate in area gh9 of review nt8. Expanded verification passed 123 tests across 20 files, covering host/session/settings/tab boundaries and terminal tab behavior. The earlier uncommitted-evaluation note is superseded by approval to commit.'
